  "lessons": "- **Indigenous & local community stories**: Strongly favored: First Nations advocacy, reconciliation, land stewardship, and BC/Cariboo or Saskatchewan regional news about real community life. Local sports and event listings are rejected.\n- **Environmental & climate framing**: Accepted when the angle is solutions, protection, or policy stakes (sustainable farming, climate action, environmental policy). Pure disaster coverage (wildfire tolls, smoke, heat waves, tornado counts), EV ownership-decline or market-share stories, and lifestyle framing are rejected.\n- **Science & nature discovery**: Favored for surprising natural phenomena, evolutionary and animal biology, astronomy, space, geoscience, and biological or medical breakthroughs; novel-tech science (micro-drones, materials) is welcome. Wellness pseudoscience and symptom-focused health advice are rejected.\n- **AI & tech: critical or substantive angles**: Accepted for security vulnerabilities, attacks on AI systems, infrastructure significance, societal-risk warnings from experts, and critiques of censorship or bias. Launches, model hype, funding and valuation news, product comparisons, and speculative fiction are rejected.\n- **Privacy & security how-tos**: Practical, user-empowering guidance (protecting accounts, spotting scams, defending against cybercrime) is valued. Product roundups, deals, subscription price tips, and gadget optimization are rejected.\n- **Journalism & institutional accountability**: Valued for press freedom, government transparency, corporate or antitrust accountability, and regulatory challenges. Sensational crime, celebrity or entertainment news, violence, and tragedy-driven stories are rejected.\n- **Local governance & civic life**: Favored for municip",
